jobs.description:
Position Summary

You may be working in a commercial law firm, and enjoy the challenge of taking on some matters autonomously, seeking guidance and support as required.

Job Requirement

You should have:

- Relevant ECM internship/work experience;
- Excellent interpersonal skills and can deliver excellent client service;
- Good analytical skills and attention to details;
- Fluency in English and Mandarin required (spoken and written);
- Immediate availability is highly preferred

Note: we do not accept agency referral for this

Responsibilities:

- Draft and prepare correspondence, agreements and other legal documents;
- Research legal issues and case law and / or examination of documentation and / or factual investigation;
- Review tender documents and other contractual documents and advising on potential legal risks;
- Assist with preparation of court bundles and other document management tasks;
- Assist in preparing briefs to external counsel, attending court and assisting external counsel;
- Liaise with government agencies; and
- Assist with general legal matters.

Requirements:

- Degree in Law from a university in Hong Kong or another common law jurisdiction;
- At least 3 years' experience working in a solicitors' firm or in-house team, ideally in construction;
- Strong initiative, organizational and problem solving skills;
- Strong personal, communication and teamwork skills;
- Determination to produce top quality work within deadline and under pressure;
- High commitment, including readiness to work late at short notice if needed;
- Willingness to learn and adapt;
- Excellent communication skills in both written and spoken English and Chinese.

Benefits:

- Competitive pay
- Discretionary bonus
- MPF top-up
- Medical insurance
- Life insurance

We are an equal opportunity employer. Information provided will be treated in strict confidence for recruitment purposes only. Candidates not being invited for interview within 6 weeks after submission date may assume their application unsuccessful. All personal data collected will be retained for a period of no more than 24 months, and destroyed afterwards. We are committed to comply with the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance of Hong Kong (the “Ordinance”) and a copy of our Personal Information Collection Statement can be accessed by visiting our Company website (www.gammonconstruction.com).

